9.375, 50.4\nq2 class1: 0.504, 0.8, 1.28, 1.6, 2.56, 6.3, 10, 16, 25, 25, 40, 63, 63, 80.64\nq3 class1: 63, 100, 160, 250, 400, 630, 1000, 1600, 2500, 2500, 4000, 6300, 6300, 6300\nq4 class1: 78.75, 125, 200, 312.5, 500, 787.5, 1250, 2000, 3125, 3125, 5000, 7875, 7875, 7875\nratio class1: 200, 200, 200, 250, 250, 160, 160, 160, 160, 160, 160, 160, 160, 125\n\nclass2 order (18): DN50, DN50 RB, DN65, DN65 RB, DN80, DN80 RB, DN100, DN100 RB, DN125, DN150, DN200, DN250, DN300, DN350, DN400, DN450, DN500, DN600\n\nq1: 0.315, 0.158, 0.5, 0.25, 0.8, 0.4, 1, 0.63, 1.6, 2.52, 6.4, 6.4, 10, 10, 16, 25.2, 25.2, 40\nq2: 0.504, 0.25, 0.8, 0.4, 1.28, 0.64, 1.6, 1.00→1.0, 2.56, 4.032, 10.24, 10.24, 16, 16, 25.6, 40.32, 40.32, 64\nq3: 63, 63, 100, 100, 160, 160, 250, 250, 400, 630, 1600, 1600, 2500, 2500, 4000, 6300, 6300, 10000\nq4: 78.75, 78.75, 125, 125, 200, 200, 312.5, 312.5, 500, 787.5, 2000, 2000, 3125, 3125, 5000, 7875, 7875, 12500\nratio: 200, 400, 200, 400, 200, 400, 250, 400, 250, 250, 250, 250, 250, 250, 250, 250, 250, 250\n\nNow attribute names: use q1 (minimum flow rate), q2 transitional, q3 permanent, q4 overload, ratio_q3_q1, diameter_inlet_outlet. Snake_case canonical.\n\nmatrix_tables rows use keys: meter_size, diameter_inlet_outlet, q1, q2, q3, q4, ratio_q3_q1. For RB rows meter_size: \"DN50 RB\" and footnote_markers [\"*\"].\n\nThis is a big JSON. Let me write it carefully.\n\nAlso should matrix_tables column_units be included? Schema shows columns[], rows[], description, footnotes[]. The R137 example includes column_units. I'll include column_units.\n\nDate formats: use ISO dates.\n\ncertificate.number: \"R49/2013-A-NL1-21.03\" — include revision separately? number field: keep \"R49/2013-A-NL1-21.03\"; revision in revision_history.\n\nLet me now write the final JSON. Also note footnote marker in markdown is \"\\*\" — marker \"*\" or \"1)\"-style. Use \"*\".\n\nAlso \"T50 (+0,1 °C / +50 °C)\": min 0.1.\n\nDouble-check DN600 class1 Q1 \"50,400\" → 50.4 and Q2 \"8